+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a category currently cascades into deleting products that belonged to it, which breaks stock and catalog data as well as carts and orders that reference those products. The category endpoint also does not reliably expose a deleted or unknown category as a clean 404, so deletion must become category-only and API behavior must be made consistent.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Delete only the requested category and all descendants; never delete products, product inventory, prices, cart items, or order items.
+- Remove deleted and descendant categories from product-category associations while retaining every product and its other category associations.
+- Make reads and product filtering treat deleted categories as absent: category lookup and deletion of an unknown category return HTTP 404, category listings omit deleted categories, and product listing by a deleted category is empty.
+- Preserve existing product, cart, and order behavior after category deletion, including product detail category output and checkout/order retrieval.
+- Add regression coverage for root and descendant deletion, multi-category products, product-only-in-deleted-category retention, missing-category 404s, and cart/order continuity.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `category-deletion`: Safe deletion of category trees and removal of their product associations without deleting products or dependent commerce records.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The category service/facade and v1 category and product APIs are affected, along with the catalog persistence relationship handling. Integration and service tests will exercise product, cart, and order flows across category deletion. No database migration or public endpoint shape change is required.
