+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Provides safe category-tree deletion that removes catalog classification without removing products or commerce records that depend on those products.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Category deletion preserves products and associations outside the deleted tree
+The system SHALL delete the requested category and its descendants while retaining every affected product, its inventory and pricing, and all category associations outside the deleted tree.
+
+#### Scenario: Product belongs only to the deleted category
+- **WHEN** a category containing a product as its only category is deleted
+- **THEN** the product remains available with its stock, price, and other product data unchanged, and has no deleted category association
+
+#### Scenario: Product belongs to deleted and surviving categories
+- **WHEN** a category tree is deleted and a product belongs to both that tree and another category
+- **THEN** the product remains available and retains the surviving category association while all deleted-tree associations are removed
+
+#### Scenario: Descendant category is deleted with its ancestor
+- **WHEN** a category with one or more descendant categories is deleted
+- **THEN** the ancestor and every descendant are deleted, and products formerly assigned to any of them are retained under the same rules
+
+### Requirement: Commerce records remain usable after category deletion
+The system SHALL not delete or invalidate cart items, order items, stock, or product pricing when a category or category tree is deleted.
+
+#### Scenario: Existing cart contains an affected product
+- **WHEN** a category containing a cart product is deleted
+- **THEN** the cart can still be read and changed and the product can still be checked out using its existing commerce data
+
+#### Scenario: Existing order contains an affected product
+- **WHEN** a category containing an ordered product is deleted
+- **THEN** the order can still be opened and its order product remains available
+
+### Requirement: Deleted categories are absent from public category and product-filter reads
+The system SHALL return HTTP 404 Not Found for a deleted or nonexistent category lookup and category deletion, omit deleted categories from category collections, and return no products when filtering by a deleted category id.
+
+#### Scenario: Read deleted category by id
+- **WHEN** a client requests GET `/api/v1/category/{id}` after that category was deleted
+- **THEN** the response is HTTP 404 Not Found
+
+#### Scenario: Delete nonexistent category
+- **WHEN** a client sends DELETE `/api/v1/private/category/{id}` for an id that does not exist
+- **THEN** the response is HTTP 404 Not Found and no product or commerce data is changed
+
+#### Scenario: List categories after deletion
+- **WHEN** a client requests GET `/api/v1/category`
+- **THEN** the response does not contain the deleted category or any of its descendants
+
+#### Scenario: List products by deleted category
+- **WHEN** a client requests GET `/api/v1/products?category={id}` for a deleted category id
+- **THEN** the response contains no products
+
+### Requirement: Product details expose only surviving category associations
+The system SHALL omit deleted and descendant categories from the category collection returned by GET `/api/v2/product/{sku}` while retaining the product itself.
+
+#### Scenario: Read product after category deletion
+- **WHEN** a client requests a product by SKU after one or more of its categories were deleted
+- **THEN** the response includes the product and only its remaining categories
