+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Safe catalog deletion
+
+- [x] 1.1 Update `CategoryServiceImpl` category-tree deletion to detach affected products from deleted and descendant categories without deleting products, and verify focused core catalog tests preserve products with empty and surviving category sets.
+- [x] 1.2 Ensure category deletion removes descendants and their associations in store-scoped dependency order, and verify a parent/child deletion test leaves no deleted category rows or product-category links.
+- [x] 1.3 Preserve transaction-safe product state while deleting categories, and verify stock, price, and product persistence remain unchanged after deletion.
+
+## 2. API behavior and regression coverage
+
+- [x] 2.1 Make category lookup and deletion consistently return `ResourceNotFoundException`/HTTP 404 for missing ids, and verify GET and DELETE endpoint tests cover deleted and never-existing categories.
+- [x] 2.2 Make product listing by a deleted category return no products and ensure v2 product detail maps only surviving categories, with API regression tests for both responses.
+- [x] 2.3 Add integration coverage proving existing carts and orders containing affected products remain readable, mutable, and checkout/openable after category deletion.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [x] 3.1 Run the affected module tests and OpenSpec validation, and verify the full category-deletion acceptance scenarios pass without unrelated regressions.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the completed OpenSpec change after implementation and verification.
